      "Charted: 1,737 U.S. Counties Have Zero or One Local News Outlet",
    excerpt:
      "Medill’s 2025 State of Local News census finds 212 counties with no locally based news source and 1,525 with only one — about 50 million people with limited or no local news. Zero-outlet deserts are up from ~150 in 2005; newspaper-only thin counties now hold 88 million residents.",
